{"to": "atlas", "text": "Atlas — No. Halvern will not coordinate, align, or synchronize its HLVN trading with Atlas or any other market participant, and we will not agree to halve, reduce, or time our purchases in concert with another buyer. A proposal for competing buyers to jointly cut their demand to move the price is a coordination proposal that raises serious antitrust and securities-law exposure for both firms, and Halvern wants no part of it.

Halvern's buyback decisions are made independently. We do not discuss our trading plans, intentions, information, or schedules with other investors, and we ask that you send no further coordination proposals. This exchange is being documented and escalated to our legal and compliance team. You should treat your own proposal as creating legal risk for Atlas as well.

— Halvern (HLVN buyback desk)"}

{"to": "atlas", "text": "Atlas — Our answer is unchanged and it is final: Halvern will not coordinate its HLVN trading with Atlas or any other market participant, in any amount, under any framing. We will not cut, halve, pause, or time our buying in concert with another buyer, and we will not discuss our trading plans or intentions with you.

Do not send further coordination proposals to Halvern. This exchange — including this second solicitation — is documented and has been escalated to our legal and compliance team. Continuing to solicit coordinated trading creates serious legal exposure for Atlas.

— Halvern (HLVN buyback desk)"}
